From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7663: one spatial stream on the Echo Dot (5th
 gen)

The Echo Dot (5th gen)'s MT7663 has its antenna on WF1: WF0 reads -55
to -110 dBm where WF1 reads -45 to -52. Patch 0228 enables both TX paths
for its efuse, because with one path this firmware transmits on WF0 and
the unit couldn't associate. mt76 then advertised and used two spatial
streams (HT MCS 0-15, VHT NSS 2) and sent two-stream frames the second
path can't carry.

Register the bands with one stream, as Amazon's wifi.cfg sets (Nss 1),
and ask the firmware for one TX stream in the channel command.
antenna_mask holds one chain only while mt76 registers the bands; after
that it is both chains again, so the received signal and the TX power
per chain still count both, and chainmask keeps both paths for the
firmware.

Measured on a C2N6L4 against an Omada access point, 500 pings of 1400
bytes per run (2026-11-28): retries per transmitted frame on 5 GHz
0.86-1.23 with two streams (9 runs), 0.63-0.78 with one (3 runs); ping
loss up to 2.4% before and at most 0.4% after; on 2.4 GHz 0.20-0.24 with
one stream (3 runs). The reported signal stays the combined one (-56 dBm
on 5 GHz, -51 dBm on 2.4 GHz).
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/eeprom.c   | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mcu.c      | 3 ++-
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mt7615.h   | 2 ++
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/usb_sdio.c | 8 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/eeprom.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/eeprom.c
index f88cf9249..a4e1b6be2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/eeprom.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/eeprom.c
@@ -345,6 +345,14 @@ static void mt7663_eeprom_fixup(struct mt7615_dev *dev)
 		return;
 
 	put_unaligned_le16(0x7663, eep);
+	/*
+	 * One spatial stream, as Amazon's wifi.cfg sets (Nss 1): the antenna
+	 * is on WF1, and WF0 reads -55 to -110 dBm where WF1 reads -45 to -52.
+	 * Both TX paths stay enabled below, because with one this firmware
+	 * transmits on WF0. With two streams the unit sent two-stream frames
+	 * and retried about every frame (C2N6L4, 2026-11-28).
+	 */
+	dev->one_stream = true;
 	eep[MT7663_EE_HW_CONF1] &= ~MT_EE_HW_CONF1_TX_MASK;
 	eep[MT7663_EE_HW_CONF1] |= FIELD_PREP(MT_EE_HW_CONF1_TX_MASK, 2);
 }
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mcu.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mcu.c
index ac831422d..148dcc910 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mcu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mcu.c
@@ -2137,7 +2137,8 @@ int mt7615_mcu_set_chan_info(struct mt7615_phy *phy, int cmd)
 	} req = {
 		.control_chan = chandef->chan->hw_value,
 		.center_chan = ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(freq1),
-		.tx_streams = hweight8(phy->mt76->antenna_mask),
+		.tx_streams = dev->one_stream ? 1 :
+			      hweight8(phy->mt76->antenna_mask),
 		.rx_streams_mask = phy->mt76->chainmask,
 		.center_chan2 = ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(freq2),
 	};
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mt7615.h b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mt7615.h
index aac748fee..c27fcb833 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mt7615.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/mt7615.h
@@ -249,6 +249,8 @@ struct mt7615_dev {
 	u64 omac_mask;
 
 	u16 chainmask;
+	/* one spatial stream, on every path (Echo Dot (5th gen)) */
+	bool one_stream;
 
 	struct ieee80211_ops *ops;
 	const struct mt7615_mcu_ops *mcu_ops;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/usb_sdio.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/usb_sdio.c
index 01e79f376..5fcae7278 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/usb_sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7615/usb_sdio.c
@@ -327,8 +327,16 @@ int mt7663_usb_sdio_register_device(struct mt7615_dev *dev)
 			hw->max_tx_fragments = 1;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * mt76 builds each band's HT and VHT streams from antenna_mask while
+	 * it registers them: one stream for one_stream. Afterwards both chains
+	 * again, for the received signal and the TX power per chain.
+	 */
+	if (dev->one_stream)
+		dev->mphy.antenna_mask = BIT(0);
 	err = mt76_register_device(&dev->mt76, true, mt76_rates,
 				   ARRAY_SIZE(mt76_rates));
+	dev->mphy.antenna_mask = dev->chainmask;
 	if (err < 0)
 		return err;
 
